\section*{Unramified de Rham quantum Langlands at irrational level}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
At every complex irrational level, the full unramified twisted $D$-module categories for a connected simple group and its dual are claimed to be equivalent at levels $c$ and $-1/(rc)$, including all global-form components. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 069, 2026-10-04): Local Whittaker comparisons and the classical inputs define the candidate kernel. A weight argument controls its filtered deformation globally, and coherent extension of local pairings across marked-point collisions establishes the localization comparison and compatibility with central torsor actions.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 069, 2026-10-04): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
